text.paragraph:
• Sublingual tablet: 30 mcg tablet housed in a disposable, single-dose applicator (SDA). (
                              3
                           )

tr.td:
The concomitant use of DSUVIA and CYP3A4 inducers can decrease the plasma concentration of sufentanil [see Clinical Pharmacology (
12.3
)], resulting in decreased efficacy or onset of a withdrawal syndrome in patients who have developed physical dependence to sufentanil [see Warnings and Precautions ( 5.6
)].
After stopping a CYP3A4 inducer, as the effects of the inducer decline, the sufentanil plasma concentration will increase [see Clinical Pharmacology (
12.3
)], which could increase or prolong both the therapeutic effects and adverse reactions, and may cause serious respiratory depression.
